0. **FIREBASE services**
   - Always design and implement using FIREBASE SERVICES
   - Always design and implement any function and client code with v2 API version compatibility.
   - Always configure and deploy for europe-west1
   - Always log and alert properly if an expected service or function is not found or working as expected

**Environments**
   - Always consider STAGING as an online FIREBASE application used for test (staketrack-dev)
   - Always consider PRODUCTION as an online FIREBASE application (staketrack). 
   - Always consider DEVELOPMENT as a local environment running on emulator
   - Never implement environment-specific code. Code should work based on environment configuration without any hard-coded differentiation.
   - Never implement environment-specific failovers

**CODE PRACTICES**
   - Always use good practices for secret management. Do not rely on static files or hard-coded properties when deploying the web-application.
   - Always store any sensitive key on _.env.[environment].local_ file in the root folder. These files are not commited to git.
   - Always store Non-sensitive keys on _.env.[environment]_ file in the root folder. These files are commited to git.
   - Always double check that .env files for different environments are kept with the same keys and organization to facilitate configuration and setup. Preserve existing values when updating existent keys.
   - Always update the .env.local.example file for proper documentation when changing the structure on any _.env.[environment].local_ file
   - Never duplicate properties for the same environment and use only the files in the root folder. do not create any _.env_ file on any other folder.
   - Always review values and keys to avoid conceptual duplication. Example: if two variables refer to the ENVIRONMENT name, ensure you rely on one key only. Configure tools and libraries properly.

**DOCUMENTATION**
_docs/spec_ are functional specifications in the EPIC-FEATURE-USER Story format
_docs/spec/tests_ are functional test specifications
_MD_ files are used to provide architectural and implementation documentation
*ALWAYS* Review specifications, tests, and documentation when implementing changes

**AUTOMATION**
_gitflow_ Automate scripts for gitflow set up using env files, using environment variables for _.env.[environment].local_ for both STAGING and PRODUCTION separately. 
Configure gitflow to use the STAGING branch to trigger STAGING deployment
Configure gitflow to use the HEAD branch to trigger PRODUCTION deployment
Create and keep npm scripts updated to deploy and configure application and projects on FIREBASE
Create and keep VSCode workspace configuration to run and debug

**TESTING**
Implement and update unit tests
Implement and update functional tests

**FUNCTIONAL**
When using the not logged in option, disable all backend dependencies except for the Analytic capabilities. Rely on local-storage to save user properties and records.
This application must be responsive and mobile-friendly.

